# Chapter 15

# Page Registry

## Overview

One of the major architectural improvements was introducing a centralized Page Registry.

Instead of every page calling its own JavaScript, pages register themselves.

File Location

```text
wwwroot/js/core/page-registry.js
```

---

# Responsibilities

The Page Registry is responsible for:

* Registering pages
* Initializing the current page
* Returning the current page
* Checking whether a page exists
* Destroying page instances

Supported methods

```text
register()

initialize()

exists()

current()

destroy()
```

---

# Registration Process

Each page registers itself.

Example

```javascript
PageRegistry.register("login", LoginPage);
```

Another example

```javascript
PageRegistry.register("dashboard", DashboardPage);
```

This allows the registry to initialize only the active page.

---

# MVC Integration

Every MVC View specifies its page name.

Example

```csharp
@{
    ViewData["Page"] = "login";
}
```

The layout copies this value to the body element.

```html
<body data-page="login">
```

The Page Registry reads this value.

Flow

```text
ViewData["Page"]

↓

Body data-page

↓

PageRegistry

↓

LoginPage.initialize()
```

This eliminates manual page initialization.

---

# Benefits

The Page Registry provides several advantages.

* One startup process
* No duplicate initialization
* Cleaner pages
* Easier debugging
* Better scalability

